/**
 * Day 97 — Phase 5 country pack 6, South Asia: India refinement (ROADMAP item 6, fifth country).
 *
 * Before this, India before 1815 was drawn only by the schematic rings of the great empires: the
 * Maurya, Kushan, Gupta, Delhi, Mughal, Maratha and British `india-*` rings, the Chola `tamil-core`
 * and `coromandel` rings and the Portuguese `goa-fringe`. Between them the Deccan, the south, Odisha,
 * Kashmir and Assam were empty for centuries or wrongly covered by an empire's ring (the Gupta and
 * Delhi rings over the whole Deccan, the Mughal ring over the far south from 1565, the Chola ring
 * over the Pallava and Pandya countries from 350). This pack adds 26 regional kingdoms and sultanates
 * from the Satavahanas (c. 100 BCE) to the Ahom kingdom (to 1813). The nations layer draws India
 * (id `india`, from 1815/1914); this pack uses other ids and has no keyframe after 1813.
 *
 * How it is built (docs/DATA.md, "Country-pack globe backfill"):
 *  - 23 new pieces from Natural Earth 1:10m admin-1 (public domain): Indian states, some split by
 *    longitude or latitude (Uttar Pradesh at 80.5°E, Madhya Pradesh into Malwa and Gwalior,
 *    Maharashtra at 77°E, Andhra into the coast and Rayalaseema, Karnataka into north, middle,
 *    south-west and south-east, Tamil Nadu into north, the Kaveri delta and the south, Assam at
 *    92.6°E), clipped to the land and to the Pakistan, Bangladesh and Nepal pieces already on the
 *    stack. Punjab, Himachal, Uttarakhand, Bihar, West Bengal, eastern Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh,
 *    Jharkhand, Kerala, Goa, the north-east hill states and the islands are not drawn by the pack
 *    (some are cut off the empire rings, see the fixes). Generator: et-tools day97-pieces.py.
 *  - A polity is a dated list of pieces; every change is a one-year step.
 *  - Every polity has a certainty level and sources, and links the India timeline items.
 *
 * Not drawn (timeline items and pins only): the Mahajanapadas and Sangam kingdoms; the Western
 * Kshatrapas, Vakatakas, Eastern Chalukyas, Cheras, Palas (Bihar, left to the Bangladesh pack), the
 * Chandelas, Paramaras and Kalachuris; the Tughluq Deccan (1318–1347) and the Madurai Sultanate; the
 * Lodi and Sur states; Berar and Bidar among the Deccan sultanates; the Rajput kingdoms, the Nayaks
 * of Madurai, Thanjavur and Mysore, the Wodeyars, Haidar Ali and Tipu Sultan, the Nawabs of Arcot,
 * Awadh and Bengal and the Nizam of Hyderabad (left to the Mughal, Maratha and British rings).
 */
